    <DataNode elementId="AT5G62790-MONOMER" textLabel="1-deoxy-D-xylulose-5-phosphate reductoisomerase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9XFS9" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="600" centerY="535" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana DXR&lt;/i&gt; gene was heterologously expressed in an &lt;i&gt;E. coli&lt;/i&gt; lethal mutant defective in the &lt;i&gt;dxr&lt;/i&gt; gene and shown to rescue the mutant phenotype |CITS:[12177470]|. Rescue was achieved with two truncated version of the &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis DXR&lt;/i&gt; gene: a long version missing some of the N-terminal region (residues 55-477) and a shorter version missing the entire N-terminal region (residue 81-477) |CITS:[12177470]|. Importantly however, the longer version led to a more vigorous growth of the rescued cells, demonstrating that the N-terminal proline-rich region (residues 57-80) contains elements that are important for activity or stability of the protein when expressed in &lt;i&gt;E. coli&lt;/i&gt;.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT5G62790-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT5G62790.2" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="Q9XFS9" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Pid" value="NP_201085" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-12475" />
      <Property key="GOTerms" value="GO:0009507" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT5G62790.2" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT5G62790" />
      <Property key="^citations" value="12177470" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <Property key="Locations" value="CCI-CHLOROPLAST-PL" />
      <Property key="MolecularWeightExp" value="46." />
      <Property key="MolecularWeightKd" value="46." />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_0012177470" />
    </DataNode>
    <DataNode elementId="AT2G34630-MONOMER" textLabel="dimethylallyltranstransferase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="O64684" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="750" centerY="535" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt; protein encoded by the &lt;i&gt;GPPS&lt;/i&gt; gene was expressed in &lt;i&gt;E. coli&lt;/i&gt;. Extracts of the bacteria recombinantly expressing the heterologous protein were shown to catalyze the condensation of DMAPP and IPP into GPP |CITS:[11069698]|. The protein fused to the reporter GFP was shown to localize in the chloroplasts of &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis&lt;/i&gt; leaves. The enzyme was not able to accept any other allylic diphosphate substrates (GPP, FPP, GGPP) for prenyl condensation |CITS:[11069698]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT2G34630-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT2G34630.2" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="O64684" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Pid" value="NP_850234" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="dimethyallylpyrophosphate transferase" />
      <Property key="Synonym_2" value="GPP synthase" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-33278, RXN-12514" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="2" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT2G34630.2" />
      <Property key="FunctionalAssignmentStatus" value=":PROBABLE-ENZYME" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT2G34630" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <Property key="MolecularWeightExp" value="36." />
      <Property key="MolecularWeightKd" value="36." />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_11069698" />
    </DataNode>
    <DataNode elementId="AT4G15560-MONOMER" textLabel="1-deoxy-D-xylulose-5-phosphate synthase, chloroplastic" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q38854" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="900" centerY="535" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana CLA1&lt;/i&gt; gene was heterologously expressed in &lt;i&gt;E. coli&lt;/i&gt; as a fusion protein (GST-CLA1). The fusion protein was tested for its ability to catalyze the formation of 1-deoxy-D-xylulose 5-phosphate (DXP) in the presence of pyruvate and glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate and thereby confirmed the DXP synthase activity of the protein |CITS:[10982425]|. Additionally, the mutant plants &lt;i&gt;cla1-1&lt;/i&gt; display an albino phenotype (no chlorophyll production) which can be partially rescued by the supplementation of synthetic, non-phosphorylated DX (1-deoxy-D-xylulose) in the growth medium |CITS:[10982425]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT4G15560-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT4G15560.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="Q38854" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Pid" value="NP_193291" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="1-deoxyxylulose-5-phosphate synthase" />
      <Property key="Synonym_2" value="DXP synthase" />
      <Property key="Synonym_3" value="DXPS" />
      <Property key="Synonym_4" value="CLOROPLASTOS ALTERADOS 1" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-12474" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT4G15560.1" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT4G15560" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_10982425" />
    </DataNode>
    <DataNode elementId="AT2G18640-MONOMER" textLabel="Geranylgeranyl pyrophosphate synthase 4" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9SLG2" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="615" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt; gene &lt;i&gt;GGPS4&lt;/i&gt; when expressed in recombinant &lt;i&gt;E.coli&lt;/i&gt; was shown to encode for a protein catalyzing the condensation of farnesyl pyrophosphate (FPP) and isopentenyl pyrophosphate (IPP) to produce geranylgeranyl diphosphate (GGPP) |CITS:[10759500]|. &lt;i&gt;In planta&lt;/i&gt;, this geranylgeranyl pyrophosphate synthase was shown to be localized in the endoplasmic reticulum of epidermal cells and leaf guard cells, most likely in its membrane |CITS:[10759500]|.</Comment>
